# Test: OSPFv2 TE LSA decode (RFC 3630, spec-ospf-ext-2).
#
# VALIDATES: a TE opaque LSA (Opaque type 1) encodes, decodes with a valid Fletcher
# checksum, splits its Link State ID to Opaque type 1, and its body decodes to a Link TLV
# with 4-byte-aligned sub-TLVs (the CLI decode path).
# PREVENTS: a byte-order slip in the LS-ID split or a mis-padded TE TLV body.

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=go test -v ./internal/plugins/ospf -run TestOSPFTEDecodeFunctional -count=1:timeout=60s
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=PASS
